WEBVTT

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.570
"Police"

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:47.050
<i>Let's chase our dreams...</i>

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.130
<i>... holding hearts burning...</i>

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.530
<i>... like the summer sunshine.</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>If we have courage...</i>

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:03.630
<i>... at 100 miles an hour...</i>

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:11.740
<i>... I'm sure the door will open.</i>

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:18.890
<i>Since sadness is the road</i>
<i>that leads to smiles...</i>

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:27.600
<i>... dull, dingy shoes will</i>
<i>start to shine, too.</i>

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:34.300
<i>The most wonderful dream</i>
<i>in the world...</i>

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:41.010
<i>The pounding beat speeds up.</i>

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:48.180
<i>The eyes are prisms that</i>
<i>catch the wind...</i>

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:55.960
<i>... and in the voices of</i>
<i>countless friends...</i>

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:02.800
<i>... I feel happiness.</i>

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.670
FILE. 1
AND SO THEY MET

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.170
As of this moment, fifteen minutes
late already, I see...

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.550
I'll go for it.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.830
Let it slide! Please!

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.610
I guess not, after all.
In that case...

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.160
Whew...

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.260
She couldn't have chased
me this far.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.470
N... No way...

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:27.550
"Police"

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.850
It ain't fair if all that counts is speed!
I'm gonna get caught!

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.350
A temple?!

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:36.880
My lucky day!

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.350
Charge!

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.590
Go! Go!

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.600
I'm impressed. But it looks like
she's reached her limit.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.800
Heave! Heave! Heave-HO!

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.970
NATSUMI POWER BOOST ON!

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:03.210
DASH! Left-right! Left-right!

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.780
Eh?!

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.220
Fine!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.020
In hopes that I can do well
at my new workplace.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:30.270
"Oshou:" in Buddhism, the priest in charge of a temple.
Oshou! Oshou! You sure are
lively, considering the heat.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.540
Oh, it's nothing.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.610
I'm in a hurry, so I'll
catch you later!

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:53.530
Whew! I thought I was a goner.
What's the time?

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.690
Nine... Wha?

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:19.460
There! Hey, kitty, that was pretty
dangerous, you know!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.360
Even though you're lucky
it was me passing by...

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:26.730
...you were on the verge of becoming
today's first accident fatality! Hmm?

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.560
Oh! You're hungry,
huh? OK, OK...

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:35.670
Huh? What?!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.670
Gone... It's gone...

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:44.080
My lunch... My lunch!

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:48.680
And now, the question;

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.790
How many moving violations
did you commit?

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:54.330
"Score:"

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:55.660
Use of an area prohibited to motor traffic.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:55.730
"Score:"

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.530
Changing lanes in a no-passing zone.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:57.600
"Score:"

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.100
Disobeying traffic signs.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:06:59.170
"Score:"

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.530
Disregarding instructions of an officer.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:01.600
"Score:"

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.900
And... exceeding the speed limit, too.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.500
<i>"Suspension of License"</i>

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:11.510
The posted legal speed is 30 kph, so
that puts you 25 kph over...

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.780
...but in deference to kitty,
I'll let it slide.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:21.550
So if you would kindly
sign here...

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:23.020
...Ms. Natsumi Tsujimoto!

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.780
Huh? How do you
know my name?

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.760
Welcome to Bokuto Precinct!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.860
"Bokuto Police Station"

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.600
Natsumi Tsujimoto!

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.400
Yes, sir!

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:41.030
As of today, you are a policewoman
of Bokuto Precinct. Is that clear?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:41.430
Yes, sir!

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.310
And on your first day of duty, you're
an hour and ten minutes late.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:45.970
Incorrect, sir.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:46.580
Hmm?

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:49.080
An hour and twelve
minutes, sir.

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:50.340
That's some nerve
you've got.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:52.420
People say that to me
all the time, sir!

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:57.050
In any case, if you have an
excuse, I'll hear it. Well?

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:58.320
Yes, sir, I do!

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:03.260
The truth is, today, I actually got the
fried egg for lunch done really well.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.990
And when I went to give it to the old lady
next door, she was so psyched!

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.330
She went on about how I just had
to become her grandson's bride.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.560
But her grandson is
still only seven...

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.000
...so she gave me lots of pickled
vegetables by way of thanks...

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.670
...and I was re-soaking them when
I looked at my watch...

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:17.040
...and suddenly it was
eight o'clock!

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.080
I raced like mad to get myself together,
and when I got on my RZ...

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.270
...wouldn't you know it, the
engine wouldn't turn over!

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:23.410
And it was just fine
yesterday, too!

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.320
But that's A-OK! I have a Moto-Compo,
y'know! And it's in top condition!

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.910
If I really pushed it, I'd be on time!
Am I lucky or what?!

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:32.460
But I wasn't going to
get off that easily!

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.420
No sooner did I hit Mito Boulevard,
then, of all things!

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:37.650
Pun on "Mito Koomon," a famous TV samurai.
You ran into Lord Koomon's
entourage, I presume?

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:43.600
Eh? Oh, wow. Making a joke that
far off must be a kind of genius, sir!

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:47.970
And?

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:52.140
At any rate, I, Natsumi Tsujimoto, was
late, but I will give my all for my duty.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:57.210
In the name of love, courage, and justice,
I will protect the people! That is all!

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.650
All right! Welcome aboard!

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.410
Oh, thank you.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.350
My fellow officers, I, Natsumi Tsujimoto...

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.260
...hope that we will work
well together. Huh?

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:12.120
As she says. I want you all to help
her out wherever necessary.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:13.820
Kobayakawa, come
here for a sec.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.230
Yes, sir.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:21.870
This is Miyuki Kobayakawa. She too was
just assigned here this past spring.

00:09:21.980 --> 00:09:24.470
Starting today, she will
be your partner.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.440
Miyuki Kobayakawa.
How do you do?

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.050
Partner?!

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.890
You've got real nerve.
I like that.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.420
Here we go...

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.320
I'm getting to like it here, too.

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:45.420
It looks like this is a happening
place, and it feels right to me.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.000
I like the way you talk. I'm Ken
Nakajima, motorcycle patrol.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:52.270
People call me the "White Hawk
of Bokuto." How do you!

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:00.140
Nakajima, Yoriko, I have some things
to do, so take over for me, OK?

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:04.440
Oh, I'll fix those binoculars
for you. Later...

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:06.850
Uh, yeah...

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:11.190
You see, Nakajima
has a thing for...

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.020
I can hear you, Yoriko.

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:13.890
Oops!

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.120
There's too much you don't
know, Nakajima.

00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:40.740
Sorry.

00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:42.850
There seems to be
a lot to remember.

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:47.360
Oh, excuse me for a sec. I've got to talk
about something. With my partner.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:53.090
Hey! What're you doing
to my bike?

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:56.100
You wiped out pretty
badly this morning!

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.230
The kickstarter was broken, and
you were leaking oil, too!

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:02.710
Oh, I put in new wires
and plugs.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.210
Give it proper maintenance
from now on, OK?

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:08.010
And I tinkered around with
various other things too...

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:10.340
...but this time it's a special
job, on the house.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.650
Oh! I'm so lucky!

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:18.420
...NOT! I mean, what's the big idea,
checking up on a person like that?

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.360
How much do you
know about me?

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.360
Let's see, career history,
special skills...

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.360
...and performance evaluations from your
previous postings... as of now, that is.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.660
Is that all? Then you don't know about
when I was in school, and...

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:31.740
...I worked my butt off to support
my motorbike hobby...

00:11:31.840 --> 00:11:33.930
...or that in school I was known
as the queen of tardiness...

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.130
...and the eating monster...
Ah, I see, I see.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.640
I'll put that in your data file.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:45.810
Why are you going over my background
like that? What am I to you?

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.220
My partner, of course.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.030
What're you looking
at, Nakajima?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.230
The birds. I'm bird watching.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:07.430
Oh? Birds are wearing uniforms
these days, eh?

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:10.440
Wh... What are you talking
about, Yoriko?!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.510
It's not like I'm interested
in Kobaya!

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:17.950
Aw, you're too easy to trip up, Nakajima.
It's just no fun at all.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.550
Do me a favor, and don't spread
any weird rumors, OK?

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:23.050
I'm the tough guy, after all...

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.120
The tough guy, huh?

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:49.950
Starting today, we'll be in charge of the
area from Districts Three through Five.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:51.780
Two patrols a day, in the morning
and in the evening.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.940
In summertime, we work 'til six.
Oh, and by the way...

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:58.020
...the basement cafeteria's "A" Lunch is
full of oysters, so that'd be my pick.

00:12:58.190 --> 00:12:59.780
I don't care for oysters.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:00.650
Oh, really?

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:02.120
That and...

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:04.060
...a certain someone
right in front of me.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.360
I know it's rude, but
I'm gonna be blunt.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.700
I don't think I can make
this work out with you.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:13.800
You're the type that gets picky about
data this and data that...

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:16.500
...you crack down on traffic violations
like there was no tomorrow...

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.100
...and to top it off, you meddle
in other people's affairs.

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.080
You're completely
unlike me.

00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:25.450
Yeah, there may be no guarantees that
we'll become really good partners.

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:31.820
But there is just one thing that I can
say with certainty; I'm really...

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:35.830
...l'm really starting to like you.

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:49.470
OK, then, let's do this...

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:54.440
I'll toss this coin. If it comes up
tails, we'll talk to the Captain...

00:13:54.550 --> 00:13:58.540
...and have ourselves reassigned.
If it comes up heads...

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:00.910
...I team up with you, huh?

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:15.860
Our future... is in my hands...

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:32.120
What was that?

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.380
What was that?
Hold it, you!

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.320
Let's go after him, too!

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:39.520
Let's go after him, too!
Fine by me!

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:51.170
Captain! A red Mini is racing through
the area! It's terrible!

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.330
A red Mini...

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.710
Nakajima, Kobayakawa, and
Tsujimoto are chasing it.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.240
We've got to send out backup!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.570
Don't worry about it.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.840
Huh?

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.340
There'll be no danger from that
red Mini. We can let it be.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.850
Uh... yes, sir.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.680
You come along whenever
someone new shows up...

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:34.300
Nice going! You took that corner
like nobody's business!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.110
But it looks like you're
out of luck.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:38.410
There's construction work up
ahead. It's a dead end!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.650
That was rude!

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.030
Sand!

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:55.920
Nakajima!

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:02.410
Are you all right, Nakajima?

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.570
Just putting on a little show!
Now get after him!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.040
Uh... right.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:14.150
I'm counting on you two.

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:18.190
You bastard!

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.020
You were waiting for
us? What a jerk!

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:21.990
Unforgivable...

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.220
Huh?

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:29.670
I built that GSX-R specially... And
you go and make it wipe out...

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.740
I'll get you if it's the
last thing I do!

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:37.730
Fox calling Kittens.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:39.540
Fox? Who is this?

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:41.440
The game has begun.

00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:43.080
It's the driver
of that Mini!

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:47.350
In 120 minutes, fireworks
will go off at H8K2.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.650
Fireworks? You
can't mean!

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:51.410
Is he talking about
a time bomb?

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:56.460
Let's synchronize watches.
3... 2... 1...

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.790
Hey! What the heck's H8K2?

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:03.900
You will know that when all
the running around is over.

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:05.230
What're you after?

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.810
This is a salute to the establishment
of your new partnership.

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:10.640
How do you know
about that?

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:13.180
Besides, we still haven't decided
whether to BE partners!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:16.250
This is a game. Let's
enjoy ourselves!

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:18.780
If you like, you can even
call for backup.

00:17:18.880 --> 00:17:20.180
If you lack confidence
in yourselves, that is.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.720
"Catch me by yourselves,"
is that it?

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:27.590
You're on! We'll catch you long
before those two hours are up!

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.060
Then I wish you luck.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:34.570
Don't lose him!

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.560
I know, I know!

00:17:50.780 --> 00:17:52.340
He's heading for
the riverbed!

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:54.180
Hold on tight, OK?

00:18:01.490 --> 00:18:03.190
What is it with that Mini?

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:04.730
It's an ERA Turbo.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.730
From the outside, it's just a Mini
that's been modified a little.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:08.730
But it's a whole different
beast on the inside.

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:09.600
What do you mean?

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:11.570
I mean we're dealing with
a serious car nut.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:12.900
Then we can't beat him?

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.510
Don't worry! This car's
no slouch, either!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:16.200
Wha?

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:19.370
I've modified the Beat-type E-074
engine into a twin-cam type...

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:21.500
...and upped the displacement
to 700cc.

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.480
And with the turbo and
intercooler systems...

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.950
...the maximum engine output exceeds
100 hp. And on top of that...

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:27.920
"On top of that?"

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:30.180
There's a custom-made
nitro injector, too!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:31.980
"Nitro?!"

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:34.350
Nitro! On!

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.460
We're gonna catch you!

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.700
You tell people not to speed,
but just look at you!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:51.070
If they run, I chase them.
It's my job, after all.

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.840
You're all right.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:58.070
You're not getting away!

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:42.520
Damn! Y... You're good!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:43.490
Now's our chance!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.630
Huh?

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.030
There's a high school up ahead.
The road takes a big detour.

00:19:50.140 --> 00:19:52.330
If we play our cards right, we
can catch him in a pincer!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.470
Which means it's time for
this baby's entrance.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.510
Let's do it!

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:05.110
This baby's smoking! She
really is something!

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.180
Now I'm set!

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:12.350
Coming through!

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.360
And... take that!

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.890
Nice shot, sweetie!

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.860
Checkmate! The game
is over, Mr. Fox!

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:33.110
This area is closed to traffic.
My condolences!

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:38.810
You can't get away now!
Give yourself up!

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:46.120
WHAT?!

00:20:46.660 --> 00:20:48.060
N... Natsumi! Get him!

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:49.320
I'm on it!

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:08.900
Only thirty minutes left.

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.880
It's all over, I guess.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.150
The game of tag ends here.

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:18.550
You both did well. As a reward,
I'll give you a hint.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:24.890
The code name of your goal is "Emily."
Study your information once more.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.620
Give it everything you've got.
That is all.

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:29.760
"Emily?" A girl?

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:33.600
What did he mean by that? I'm
no good at this kind of thing!

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.330
Calm down, Miyuki.
Try to remember...

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.500
He said we'd understand when all
the running around was done...

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:43.050
When all the running
around was done...

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.120
That's it!

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:46.650
Have you figured
something out?

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:51.350
Look! I've drawn a line through
the roads we chased him over.

00:21:51.520 --> 00:21:53.390
Isn't this... an airplane?

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:03.630
Serial number H8K2, code name "Emily,"
refers to the Type Two Flying Boat.

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:06.230
Built in 1940, it was tops in the world
during WWll when it came to...

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:10.140
...speed, flight range, and waterborne
takeoffs and landings!

00:22:10.310 --> 00:22:12.040
What's that got to do
with anything?

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:14.510
There still is one now...
at Odaiba Park.

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:18.180
Only twenty minutes to go!

00:22:18.280 --> 00:22:21.880
We'll never make it using normal
roads. Find us a short cut!

00:22:21.990 --> 00:22:23.110
OK!

00:22:25.390 --> 00:22:29.490
There's a subway tunnel under
construction 500m ahead!

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:33.220
If we cut through there, it puts us directly
on Expressway Nine... the Bayshore!

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:34.630
Roger!

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:50.080
Ten minutes!

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:50.980
We gotta make it!

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:03.530
There it is... by the landing gear!

00:23:03.700 --> 00:23:05.460
Everyone! Please evacuate!

00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:06.500
This is dangerous! Please evacuate!

00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:07.120
What?

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:07.330
They said it's dangerous!

00:23:07.330 --> 00:23:08.860
Please get out of here!

00:23:08.970 --> 00:23:09.400
Hurry! Please get out of here!

00:23:09.400 --> 00:23:10.700
Only thirty seconds left!

00:23:10.800 --> 00:23:11.960
Look, you get out of here, too!

00:23:12.140 --> 00:23:12.540
Huh?

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:16.330
I can defuse this old thing.
So get out of here!

00:23:16.510 --> 00:23:21.040
Miyuki! Even for you, it's impossible!
I'll throw this thing in the ocean!

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:22.310
That's impossible, too!

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:24.780
How many meters do you think
it is to the ocean from here?

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:25.780
You can't throw it that far!

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:26.950
Look, let me handle it!

00:23:26.950 --> 00:23:28.080
Get your hands out of the way!

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:29.920
We're running out of time!

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:31.280
Time?

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:38.700
Wow! That's pretty!

00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:39.660
Fireworks?

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:51.380
"From Fox to Kittens"
"Game Over; If found, please
report to the police?"

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.740
Oh! I just
bet!
"From Fox to Kittens"

00:23:55.580 --> 00:23:59.020
It is! It's my lunch! I'm happy!

00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:03.180
Oh, is that all?

00:24:06.660 --> 00:24:08.350
How green.

00:24:24.210 --> 00:24:27.540
We went through a lot today... but
didn't it seem pretty interesting...

00:24:27.650 --> 00:24:29.240
...when all's said and done?

00:24:29.410 --> 00:24:31.540
Well, it wasn't boring,
that's for sure...

00:24:31.720 --> 00:24:36.620
Hmph. You certainly looked like you
were enjoying yourself, though.

00:24:36.790 --> 00:24:42.120
Yes, ma'am. Thanks to my top notch
partner, it was an enjoyable day.

00:24:42.290 --> 00:24:44.090
Now that's more like it.

00:24:44.200 --> 00:24:47.500
Hey, Partner, are you interested
in moving?

00:24:47.670 --> 00:24:48.690
Moving?

00:24:48.870 --> 00:24:52.000
Your present apartment is far away
and inconvenient, right?

00:24:52.100 --> 00:24:55.340
There's a nice place, very close
to Bokuto Precinct.

00:24:55.440 --> 00:25:00.540
Lots of sunshine, and a pretty,
punctual roommate, to boot.

00:25:00.650 --> 00:25:03.620
Are you by any chance suggesting
we live together?

00:25:03.720 --> 00:25:06.340
You'd benefit by not being
late anymore.

00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:07.950
What's your real motive?

00:25:08.120 --> 00:25:11.520
It's kinda unsafe for a woman
to be living alone, you know!

00:25:11.690 --> 00:25:13.520
What does that make me?

00:25:13.690 --> 00:25:15.060
My bodyguard!

00:25:16.460 --> 00:25:20.360
Oh, no! And I've still got
lunch left over, too!

00:25:20.530 --> 00:25:22.360
Okay, say ah!

00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:23.560
Ah!

00:25:27.740 --> 00:25:29.710
Salty! What is this?

00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:36.750
W... Why you...

00:25:45.690 --> 00:25:48.250
By the way, what was the outcome
of that coin toss?

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:50.260
Oh! I completely forgot.

00:25:50.400 --> 00:25:51.330
Let me do it.

00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:53.560
Sure. I'll leave it up to you.

00:25:53.730 --> 00:25:54.930
Thank you.

00:25:57.440 --> 00:25:59.100
OK then, here I go.

00:25:59.270 --> 00:26:00.360
Be my guest.

00:26:02.310 --> 00:26:10.240
How about THIS?!

00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:33.540
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

00:26:33.610 --> 00:26:42.940
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:50.890
<i>The sunset skyline flashes past</i>
<i>in my side-view mirror.</i>

00:26:50.960 --> 00:26:58.450
<i>This is the road I drive on every day,</i>
<i>believing in my dreams.</i>

00:26:58.560 --> 00:27:06.360
<i>On rainy days, windy days, and days</i>
<i>when I wanted to throw it all away...</i>

00:27:06.470 --> 00:27:14.200
<i>... you smiled as you</i>
<i>sat beside me.</i>

00:27:15.480 --> 00:27:19.990
<i>I love the unchanging vista, the sky</i>
<i>that we watch together.</i>

00:27:23.990 --> 00:27:30.800
<i>That's why I'm confident that I can</i>
<i>hang in there, if it's for you.</i>

00:27:30.860 --> 00:27:39.270
<i>I love the smile you always have.</i>
<i>With all the passion I have...</i>

00:27:39.370 --> 00:27:39.500
<i>... I will protect you from sighs.</i>

00:27:45.840 --> 00:27:45.880
<i>I love this town where we</i>
<i>happened to meet...</i>

00:28:09.130 --> 00:28:13.370
It's coming... it's coming...
There's a storm coming!

00:28:13.540 --> 00:28:17.000
S... So you're the type that gets excited
when a typhoon comes too, huh?

00:28:17.110 --> 00:28:17.910
Oh, brother!

00:28:18.080 --> 00:28:20.840
Well, of course! Water flooding,
storms thrashing...

00:28:21.010 --> 00:28:22.540
...trees falling along streets, people
crashing into windows!

00:28:22.650 --> 00:28:24.950
Streets without people!
Slippery roads!

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:28.880
And with things flying all over, danger
everywhere, it's such a joy!

00:28:28.990 --> 00:28:30.450
Er... hello?

00:28:30.560 --> 00:28:33.620
You're Under Arrest, File 2,
"Tokyo Typhoon Rally."

00:28:33.730 --> 00:28:36.630
Looks like there're others
just like you!
FILE. 2
TOKYO TYPHOON RALLY
